# Mobile/PWA vs Desktop — no bleed

Cinext has **two separate UI systems**. Desktop web work must never change mobile/PWA layout, widgets, or controls.

## Hard rules

1. **Default assumption:** Any visual/CSS/JSX change is **desktop-only** unless the user explicitly asks for mobile/PWA.
2. **Breakpoints:** Desktop chrome and layouts live under `@media (min-width: 900px)` / `matchMedia('(min-width: 900px)')`. Do not rely on CSS overrides alone to “undo” desktop markup on phones.
3. **Never** put desktop Highlights/Library/Explore layout into unscoped CSS or into tablet queries like `(min-width: 700px) and (pointer: coarse)` — those hit real phones/iPads and overwrite the PWA.
4. **Shared components** (`LibraryClient`, `highlights/page.jsx`, etc.) must render **separate trees** when layouts diverge:
   - Gate with `isDesktopHighlights` / equivalent (`min-width: 900px`), not by restyling one shared widget
   - Mobile keeps its own controls (e.g. Library **View dropdown**, not the desktop Poster/DVD **pill toggle**)
   - Desktop-only UI goes in `LibraryDesktop` / desktop CSS classes, not by replacing mobile header chrome
5. **Highlights:** Mobile tree = pre-desktop inline layout (amber glow, baseline “N hours watched”, `#131313` scrollable stat cards, liquid-glass personality, 156px posters, matte `#171717` calendar). Desktop tree = glass/ambient/stat-widget under `@media (min-width: 900px)` only. Do not share the desktop widget shell on mobile.
6. Before finishing desktop work, sanity-check: would this change appear on a 390px phone? If yes without an explicit mobile request, undo it or gate it behind `min-width: 900px` **and** a separate JSX branch.

## When the user reports mobile regression

Fix **only** the mobile/PWA path. Do not “simplify” by sharing the new desktop widget. Restore the prior mobile control/pattern.
